<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><!--
    Android Auto Backup, API 30 and below. The modern file is data_extraction_rules.xml, and both
    are needed: minSdk is 26, so wiring up only the API-31+ one would leave every older device
    backing the photo gallery up anyway.

    Only exclusions are listed, so everything else — the database, preferences, avatars/ and
    (from Phase 5) documents/ — is still covered. That is ADR-0005's evidential core, and it is
    what Auto Backup is for.

    photos/ is out because the per-app quota is ~25 MB and Android rejects the *entire* dataset when
    it is exceeded rather than trimming it: a gallery would one day take the database down with it,
    which inverts the promise this backup exists to make. The published privacy policy says so in
    words — "Your photo gallery in the app is deliberately excluded from it" — and ADR-0005 requires
    the app to say it out loud in Settings too, because a gap the owner cannot see is worse than one
    they were told about.

    preserved/ is out for a different reason (ADR-0007): it is the app's one unbounded, never-pruned
    directory, and what makes a preserved copy safe is the owner's share tap, not an automatic net.

    The -wal/-shm sidecars are deliberately *not* handled here. Excluding them would lose committed
    transactions that have not been checkpointed yet, which is worse than the mid-write capture it
    would prevent; the fix is a WAL checkpoint, and that needs the custom BackupAgent ADR-0005 puts
    at 1.0.
-->
<full-backup-content>
    <exclude domain="file" path="photos/" />
    <exclude domain="file" path="preserved/" />
</full-backup-content>
